{
 "id": "2026-11-19-cop31-draft-drops-fossil-fuels",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "The draft climate deal just shrank by half. What happened to fossil fuels?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "At COP thirty-one in Antalya, Turkey, a revised deal text came out Thursday. Reuters reports it cut both of Monday's references to fossil fuels and limiting their use. Australian media report the draft shrank from eighteen pages to nine."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Also gone, per Reuters: a target of one hundred twenty billion dollars to help poorer countries adapt. What stayed is the host's goal for electricity to cover thirty-five percent of world energy use by twenty thirty-five, plus a call to scale up carbon removal."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Mohamed Adow of Power Shift Africa said the text has gone backwards, AFP reports. Greenpeace warned carbon removal could let producers keep expanding. Talks chief Chris Bowen said it holds the strongest terms that could win approval. Talks are set to end Friday."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will fossil fuels return in the final deal? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
