  "title": "COP31's New Draft Deletes Fossil Fuels #shorts",
  "description": "At COP31 in Antalya, Türkiye, negotiators published a revised draft deal on Thursday. Reuters reports it removed both of Monday's references to fossil fuels and limiting their use, as well as a $120 billion adaptation finance target; the text was cut from 18 to 9 pages. The host's goal of electricity covering 35% of world energy use by 2035 and a call to scale up carbon removal stayed. Power Shift Africa's Mohamed Adow said the text \"has gone backwards\" (AFP); talks chief Chris Bowen said it holds the strongest terms that could win approval. Talks are set to end Friday.\n\nSources: Reuters (via Dawn, The Express Tribune, The Globe and Mail, Arab News), AFP (via The New Arab, 24NewsHD), CBC News, Yahoo News Australia (based on search-result excerpts). Map locations are for orientation.\n\n#climate #cop31 #fossilfuels #climatechange #antalya",
